menu "KVS Signaling Configuration"

    config USE_ESP_WEBSOCKET_CLIENT
        bool "Use esp_websocket_client instead of libwebsockets"
        default n if IDF_TARGET_LINUX
        default y
        help
            Kinesis Video Stream SDK uses libwebsockets for the signaling API requests.
            By using esp_websocket_client, you get better control over memory usage as the complete signaling part is re-implemented with ESP-IDF constraints in mind

    config PREFER_DYNAMIC_ALLOCS
        bool "Prefer dynamic memory allocations"
        default y
        help
            When enabled, use dynamic memory allocation for signaling payloads and URLs.
            This can reduce static memory usage but may increase heap fragmentation.
            Enable this option on platforms with limited memory to avoid large static allocations.

    config KVS_SIGNALING_WSS_PING_INTERVAL_SEC
        int "WebSocket keep-alive ping interval (seconds)"
        range 5 300
        default 10
        help
            Keep-alive cadence on the signaling WebSocket. Each ping is a radio
            transmit, so a longer interval costs less power.

            If the interval is too long, an idle NAT or AWS can drop the
            channel. The failure appears later, when a viewer offer does not
            arrive.

            The value also sets secs_since_valid_ping in the libwebsockets
            build, so both paths use one cadence.
endmenu
